WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.784 --> 00:00:16.152
Now, reader, the princess loved the lake with all her heart.

2
00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:19.954
She knew where to find its best diving spots.

3
00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:24.136
She knew where its tallest banks sat.

4
00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:29.980
She knew where all its fish and wild creatures lived.

5
00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:39.009
So, of course, Ellen knew at once that the lake was changing.

6
00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:42.990
She first noticed it while swimming with the prince.

7
00:00:44.651 --> 00:00:46.831
She shot to the surface and looked around.

8
00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:50.152
"Something's wrong with the lake!"

9
00:00:51.813 --> 00:00:53.513
The prince popped up nearby.

10
00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:56.074
"It looks fine to me."

11
00:00:56.094 --> 00:00:59.755
"No, the lake is different!"

12
00:01:00.975 --> 00:01:04.296
She took off, swimming toward a deeper part of the lake.

13
00:01:05.748 --> 00:01:08.090
He swam after her, wondering if she was sick.

14
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.171
"Ellen! Are you okay?"

15
00:01:11.412 --> 00:01:13.213
Ellen didn't reply or look back.

16
00:01:15.095 --> 00:01:19.638
Instead she darted from place to place, checking different spots around the lake.

17
00:01:28.224 --> 00:01:31.466
The next day when they met, she was even more upset.

18
00:01:31.486 --> 00:01:34.208
"The banks are too dry.

19
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.201
The grass and plants are dying."

20
00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:43.565
She pointed to rocks baking in the sun.

21
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:48.328
"Look! Those rocks are usually under the water."

22
00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:52.350
The confused prince tried to comfort her.

23
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.331
But she pushed him away.

24
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.854
is terrible," she cried.

25
00:01:59.874 --> 00:02:02.336
"The lake is losing its water!"

26
00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.630
Agnes stayed in the cellar for seven days and seven nights.

27
00:02:21.976 --> 00:02:24.838
Finally the water dragon dropped onto the floor.

28
00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:28.721
It quickly dried up and turned back to seaweed.

29
00:02:31.563 --> 00:02:33.564
The witch grabbed the seaweed and looked up.

30
00:02:38.248 --> 00:02:41.409
Water was beginning to drip from the stone.

31
00:02:41.429 --> 00:02:45.611
"The spell worked!"

32
00:02:46.271 --> 00:02:46.872
she cried.

33
00:02:47.512 --> 00:02:50.953
Soon lake water would be rushing into her cellars.

34
00:02:51.874 --> 00:02:54.535
She had to get back upstairs—fast!

35
00:02:57.556 --> 00:02:59.557
The next day Agnes checked the lake.

36
00:03:00.777 --> 00:03:02.238
Most of its water was gone.

37
00:03:03.198 --> 00:03:05.699
But here and there were a few shallow pools.

38
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:07.800
Agnes frowned.

39
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.602
"The spell is taking too long!"

40
00:03:14.184 --> 00:03:16.446
That night Agnes went back to the lake.

41
00:03:17.887 --> 00:03:21.510
She walked all around, sprinkling her potion everywhere.

42
00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:29.916
She even tossed some into the air, at the princess' window.

43
00:03:38.132 --> 00:03:42.736
An instant later the kingdom's rivers and brooks stopped flowing.

44
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:46.058
Water no longer rushed down its mountains.

45
00:03:47.039 --> 00:03:49.140
Fountains and wells went dry.

46
00:03:50.021 --> 00:03:52.123
Even babies' tears dried up.

47
00:03:53.143 --> 00:03:57.347
At the lake the last bit of water was finally gone.
